  "details": "I dunno what other Worlds cause this, but this is the only one I visited that has shown serious conflicts with the Quick Menu and HUD in terms of visibility.\n\nFor this issue, go to the world \"Picnic in Canyon\" by Rys2ard. Here's the link: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_e7da345d-776a-42b6-90f6-50fb1dc932be\n\nVisit this world. Open the Quick Menu and use Expressions on the Wings. You will see that the Color of the Buttons has greatly faded away (looks more Dark Red). This will be more prevalent on some other UI Elements in the Quick and Main Menu.\n\nNow switch worlds. You will see that this issue will not go away, no matter which world you go to... until you Restart VRChat.\n\nSee Screenshots attached. As you can see, I have VRC+ so I customized the UI colors. But this also affects the Default Theme as well, at least when I tested it. (Third picture is after I switched Worlds).\n\nI am wondering if one of the VRC Engineers can shine a light on why Shaders can conflict with the UI like this, as I know this is never supposed to be possible whatsoever. But apparently, the World I linked has bypassed this somehow.",
